      "notes": "Single entries use the voucher create route; bounded bulk batches use /imports/vouchers in Laravel shadow. The Apps Script production writer requires one stable SourceID per row and binds ClientID to bulk-<SourceID> for replay; historical Apps Script export sources and populated lifecycle/approval/original-number/receipt/vendor-type metadata fail closed before writes instead of being discarded. Apps Script remains the production writer. Laravel shadow persists a repeatable source manifest, replays matching source hashes, quarantines conflicts and unsupported historical fields, and reconciles all submitted amounts in paise. Original 1-based CSV data-row positions are carried as rows[].sourceRowNumber through 100-row chunks, included in the immutable batch manifest hash, persisted in the row ledger and returned in reconciliation; positions never reset at chunk boundaries.",
